# portable-tpcc repository rules

Full text: [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md).

## Style and analysis

- Protocol and requirements live in [`docs/specification.md`](../../docs/specification.md) (remote process contract §9.1–§9.2). Follow the specification; do not reconstruct protocol from source or from a single adapter. See [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md).
- Preserve the coding style of the directory being modified; do not perform drive-by refactoring.
- Before making changes, study the context, dependencies, and the component's `ya.make` or `go.mod`; minimize the diff.
- Build ya modules from the repository root with `./ya make …`; build and test the root `mind/` module with `go -C mind build ./cmd/mind-tpcc` and `go -C mind test ./...` (see [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) §3).
- Build YDB (`tpcc/app/ydb`) with `-DHAVE_CUDA=no -DCUDA_VERSION=11.4` (see [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) §3 “Building the YDB variant”); `./build.sh` passes these flags automatically.
- Ask the user if the task is ambiguous or requires changes in protected areas.

## Do not modify without an explicit user request

Directories: `build/`, `contrib/`, `devtools/`, `library/`, `util/`.
